Hi Nolan, thanks for checking in.

Are you running v1? This is the version that is currently on
CRAN. It offers the ability to upload your own user variables as environmental data
but does not allow user uploads for projecting. It does have capabilities to transfer
the model to a new time period using WorldClim future bioclim variables, but this only
works if you built the model using WorldClim bioclimatic variables. The future
variables need to correspond to the variables you built the model with, so if
you uploaded your own variables instead of using WorldClim, the option will
disappear.
I think this is what you meant by saying the options were
gone, but v2 (which will be on CRAN very soon!) is stable and can be installed through
GitHub. (Check out the vignette <https://wallaceecomod.github.io/wallace/articles/tutorial-v2.html> for install instructions & info on transferring to future environments).

 In v2, the module “Transfer to User Environments” can be
used to upload your own future rasters to transfer the model to. Please note: this version has updated the terminology from “project”
to the more appropriate “transfer”, since project is commonly used in GIS for
changing the map projection; "Project" in v2 is now "Transfer" in v2. To use this module, just make sure your future rasters are
named similarly to your initial rasters. (there will be a message regarding proper
naming in the window).

Let me know if this answered your question.

Bethany Johnson

